{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794183608,"nonce":"Qk3iK0tdjqTxAqFp12tasUmoTbc=","message":"Profiled with a cache benchmark (cache/display_scale_test.go: 1000 issues, about 830 of them one of 2-3 copies of a key, every copy reached; 10k filler refs; `git pack-refs --all`). Before: 1.58 s and 832 entity reads per cold open + drawing every id. 85% of IssueHumanId's time was go-git's packed-refs scan inside dag.Read (ResolveRef -\u003e findPackedRefsInFile), the rest the object reads and replay. After: 8.6 ms, 0 entity reads.\n\nDecisions this change makes (doc/design/store.md):\n\n1. \"Readers use the excerpts\" (user's invariant): anything built over the issues reads the excerpts and loads no entity; an entity is read whole only for one issue's history (`issue get`, show, `log`, a replay `--at`) and by a write. Also a bullet in AGENTS.md.\n\n2. \"The excerpt carries the reach\": the issue excerpt carries `Reaches map[namespace]Reach`, each registered hook's answer for the copy's history, and FirstReached / aliasNamed read it, so alias resolution, the drawn ids and the Jira index's consolidation load no entity. To make that possible, a reach hook is registered process-wide from an init function (`cache.RegisterReach(namespace, version, f)`; package jira registers `Reach`) in place of per-store `SetReach` / `jira.Register`, because the excerpts are built while the store opens, before a per-store hook could be given. The issue cache file records the hooks and versions it was built with (a stamp beside the format version, which goes to 6); a file built with others is rebuilt.\n   Not the raw metadata a hook reads, kept on the excerpt for the hook to run over: Jira's reads every sync marker, each a whole base, so the cache file would hold every base of every issue.\n   Not a hook given to an open store: its excerpts are already built.\n\nFirstReached's signature changes from a ReachFunc to a namespace. Winner and ambiguity rules are unchanged; a test checks that each copy's excerpt reach (built, and read back from the file) equals the hook's answer over the entity.","files":null}]}